# =====================================================================
#  Files git must never commit.
#  Anything in this folder that is NOT listed here will be published.
# =====================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#  YOUR PASSWORD FILE - THIS IS THE IMPORTANT ONE.
#  my-github-details.txt holds your GitHub token. The rule below keeps
#  it on your PC and out of GitHub, forever. Never delete these two lines.
#  The * also covers near-miss names such as "my-github-details.txt.txt"
#  or "my-github-details - Copy.txt".
#  The second line is what lets the blank EXAMPLE template - which holds
#  no secrets - stay in the project, so you always have a fresh copy.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
my-github-details*
!my-github-details.EXAMPLE.txt

# Local build output. Only appears if the build script is run by hand;
# the live site is built fresh by GitHub Actions on every push.
_site/

# Python's compiled-bytecode cache. Appears whenever the build script runs on your PC.
__pycache__/

# OS / editor junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Local AI-agent tooling. Not part of the website.
_bmad/
_bmad-chain-ext/
_bmad-output/
.claude/
